# Claim 06 — Artifact trail

## Goal
Verify a completed or attempted run persists prompts, stdout/stderr, result
JSON, attempt summaries, journals, and run state.

## Inventory (read-only) for run 5e1de960-5456-4dc2-a1c7-a1bdf231cdc6

```
RELEASE_AUDIT/README_VERIFY/_state/goals/5e1de960-5456-4dc2-a1c7-a1bdf231cdc6/
  run.json                                   (2923 B, mode 0600)
  scout/
    PLANNING_BRIEF.md                        (17616 B)  — planner system brief
    plan_draft.md                            (1552 B)   — scout draft plan
    execution_plan.json                      (2403 B)   — typed plan JSON
    scout_report.json                        ( 347 B)   — DAG nodes/edges
    planning_stdout.txt                      (2249 B)   — planner CLI stdout
    planning_stderr.txt                      (   0 B)   — planner CLI stderr
    planning_raw_output.txt                  (2249 B)   — raw model output
    attempt-1.json                           (2265 B)   — scout attempt summary
    auth_mode.txt                            ( 118 B)   — auth mode artifact
    node_specs/
      add-run-node-docstring.md              (1219 B)   — per-step planning spec
```

This run was --plan-only, so it stopped before any worker dispatch.
Therefore there is no `workers/<stepId>/` subdir yet for this run, no
WORKING.md (worker journal), and no executor `sessions/` data — those
artifacts are created only after worker dispatch begins. The directory
shape and persistence model are still verifiable through code citations
below; the run-store layout is the same regardless of phase.

