## Code path citations (how each artifact type is persisted)

- src/goal/run-store.ts:31-47 — atomicWriteJson + saveRun: run.json is
  written via temp-file + rename, chmod 0600.
- src/goal/run-store.ts:493-499 — resolveWorkingFile / resolveGoalWorkingFile:
  per-step WORKING.md lives under workers/<stepId>/WORKING.md; run-level
  WORKING.md lives at the run root.
- src/goal/attempt-bundle.ts:35-36 — resolveWorkerDir: `workers/<stepId>/`.
- src/goal/cli-worker.ts:234-235 — `mkdirSync(workerDir, { recursive: true })`
  on dispatch.
- src/goal/cli-worker.ts:273-276 — writeTextArtifact for
  `worker-prompt-<attempt>.txt`.
- src/goal/cli-worker.ts:294-295 — `attempt-<n>.stdout.txt` and
  `attempt-<n>.stderr.txt` for the worker subprocess.
- src/goal/cli-worker.ts:184-185 — `attempt-<n>.repair.stdout.txt`/`.repair.stderr.txt`
  for repair passes.
- src/goal/cli-worker.ts:250 — `writeAuthModeArtifact` for claude_code.
- src/goal/run-journal.ts:14-22 — appendGoalWorkingEntry writes to the
  run-level WORKING.md.
- src/goal/run-journal.ts:25-44 — appendRetryContext writes per-step
  WORKING.md retry sections.
- src/goal/run-journal.ts:46-78 — appendRalphContext writes ralph history
  per step (also viewable via buildRalphHistorySummary at :80).
- src/goal/planner.ts:146 — plan-raw.txt is written under the run dir on
  planner output for debugging.

## Safe README wording
- "every run persists its typed plan, per-step prompts, worker stdout/stderr,
  worker result JSON, attempt summaries, journals, and run state under a
  single run directory."
- "artifacts live under $STATE_DIR/goals/<runId>/, with worker subprocess
  output captured per attempt as plain-text files alongside a typed
  worker_result.json."

## Unsafe README wording to avoid
- "captures every stdin/stdout byte of every subprocess" (true for worker
  CLIs, but easy to overclaim).
- "writes a database log" (no DB; flat files only).

STATUS: verified
REASON: All artifact types named in the brief are persisted by the goal system. For this plan-only run, run.json plus the full scout/ artifact set (typed plan, planner stdout/stderr/raw, scout report DAG, per-step node spec, attempt summary, auth-mode audit) are present on disk. Worker-dispatch-time artifacts (workers/<stepId>/worker-prompt, attempt-<n>.stdout/stderr, worker_result.json, WORKING.md journals) are unambiguously sourced in cli-worker.ts (lines 234, 273-276, 294-295) and run-journal.ts (lines 14-78); they are not present here only because no worker ran in a plan-only flow.
